<p>NOTE: Net income on a pro forma basis (net income excluding acquisition-related charges) for the first quarter of 1997 was $4.2 million, or $.16 per share, compared to $1.2 million, or $.05 per share, in the same quarter last year.</p>
<p>Aquisition-related charges were incurred when CSG Systems, Inc., operating then as Cable Services Group, Inc., was purchased in a leveraged buy-out in November 1994.  The charges include amortization of acquired software, client contracts and related intangibles, noncompete agreement, goodwill, and stock-based employee compensation.  These non-cash charges for the first quarter of 1997 and 1996 totaled $5.5 million and $8.5 million, respectively.</p>
